# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/
out/
*.ccskin

# Per-machine launch config — holds absolute scratchpad paths, never shared
.claude/launch.json

# Owner-supplied hero source photographs (Plan 0003). Deliberately NOT tracked.
# Owner ruling 4 on that plan makes the theme built from them private and local
# only; committing the source would put the photograph into git history, where
# removing it later means rewriting history rather than deleting a file. The
# asymmetry decides it: keeping it out is trivially reversible, putting it in is
# not. Nothing in the repo may depend on these files existing — tests build
# their own inputs, and the calibration fixture under tests/fixtures/ is a
# derived copy of an image the repo already ships.
assets/hero-sources/

# D-0003-6 — the theme directory is build output; the recipe is the source.
# Deep Navy Portrait (Plan 0003 M4) is private/local only, by owner ruling 4 on
# that plan — the same ruling that keeps assets/hero-sources/ out of the repo
# above. Its staged assets are a copy of a private photograph
# (assets/hero-sources/BW_Jisoo.png), and its emitted theme.css embeds that
# same photograph as a base64 data URI, so committing anything under this
# directory — staged assets or emitted output alike — would put the
# photograph into git history by the back door, exactly what the block above
# exists to prevent. The recipe that describes this theme IS committed, at
# tools/palette/recipes/deep-navy-portrait.mjs — only the theme directory
# built from it is excluded. Rebuilding it is one command once the assets are
# staged: node tools/palette/emit-theme.mjs deep-navy-portrait
themes/deep-navy-portrait/

# D-0003-3 — The palette-directions sheet is a BUILD PRODUCT, not a committed
# mockup — the one file in docs/mockups/ that is generated rather than tracked.
# It embeds the hero images it is judging, and one of those is a private
# photograph from the ignored directory above; committing the sheet would put
# that photograph into git history by the back door, defeating the rule
# immediately above it. Owner decision, 2026-08-05. Rebuild it any time with:
#     node tools/mockup/build-palette-directions.mjs
#
# The 0006 pattern is retained deliberately even though its builder was retired
# in M3b: a stale copy of that sheet may still sit in a working tree from before
# the rename, and it embeds the same photograph, so it must stay un-committable.
docs/mockups/0006-palette-recommendation.html
docs/mockups/0007-palette-directions.html

# Scratch / temp
scratchpad/
*.log
*.tmp

# Playwright MCP session output (snapshots, console logs) — QA artefacts, not source
.playwright-mcp/

# OS cruft
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
